$ Mechanism check (PARAM MAXRATIO, BAILOUT): the square of
$ mechanism_square_crod.bdf turned 30 degrees in its plane, so that the zero
$ pivot comes out of round-off as a small nonzero number. Four CRODs, no
$ diagonal. Grid 1 is held in x and y, grid 2 in y, so the square has no rigid
$ body motion but can still shear (grids 3 and 4 move in x together with no
$ stiffness). KLL is singular although no diagonal term is zero, so AUTOSPC
$ does not remove it. The factorization of KLL should be reported as nearly
$ singular (ratio of matrix diagonal to factor diagonal > MAXRATIO), and with
$ the default BAILOUT = 0 the run should stop there.
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = SQUARE OF FOUR CRODS, NO DIAGONAL, TURNED 30 DEG (A SHEAR MECHANISM)
DISPLACEMENT = ALL
SUBCASE 1
  SPC = 1
  LOAD = 1
BEGIN BULK
GRDSET                                                  3456
GRID    1               0.0000  0.0000  0.0
GRID    2               8.6603  5.0000  0.0
GRID    3               3.6603  13.6603 0.0
GRID    4               -5.0000 8.6603  0.0
CROD    1       1       1       2
CROD    2       1       2       3
CROD    3       1       3       4
CROD    4       1       4       1
PROD    1       1       0.5
MAT1    1       1.0E7           0.3
SPC1    1       12      1
SPC1    1       2       2
FORCE   1       3               100.0   1.0     0.0     0.0
ENDDATA
